module-help "
ORCA is a general-purpose quantum chemistry software package used to calculate
the electronic structure, energetics, and spectroscopic properties of
molecules. Developed primarily by Frank Neese's group at the
Max-Planck-Institut für Kohlenforschung and distributed commercially via
FACCTs, it runs on Linux, macOS, and Windows and is free for academic use.
"
